eed a change window for the DNS switch or is it\n  covered under the existing CR? nobody was sure\n- fatima asked about SLA credits for the june outage. parked, needs commercial input\n    input meeting_context = Weekly delivery sync, ADNOC account — Ashish, Priya, Rahul, and Fatima from the client side\n    input tone = Direct\n    → Start …\n    ✓ Start (0s)\n    → Actions and Email Writer …\n    ✓ Actions and Email Writer (1m 5s)\n    → End …\n    ✓ End (0s)\n    Dify ran 3 node(s)\n\n## Decisions\n- Migration cutover moved to 28th, pending Fatima confirming with her infra team.\n\n## Actions\n| Action | Owner | Due |\n|--------|-------|-----|\n| Confirm migration cutover date of 28th with infra team | Fatima | Not set |\n| Chase network team for DR site firewall rules | Owner not assigned | Not set |\n| Follow up with procurement for the 4 licences PO | Rahul | Friday |\n| Send updated runbook | Ashish | Before cutover (28th) |\n\n## Follow-up email\n**Subject:** ADNOC Delivery Sync – Cutover Moved to 28th, Actions Needed\n\nHi Ashish, Priya, Rahul, Fatima,\n\nWe’ve moved the migration cutover to the 28th (Fatima to confirm with infra). Here are the actions from today:\n\n- Fatima: Confirm 28th cutover with your infra team.\n- Rahul: Follow up with procurement on the 4 licences PO by Friday. Budget is approved, but the PO hasn’t been received.\n- Ashish: Share the updated runbook before the cutover.\n- Firewall rules for the DR site: still missing, blocking the failover test. Someone needs to chase their network team—please assign or volunteer.\n\nTwo items are unresolved: whether the DNS switch requires a separate change window, and the SLA credits for the June outage (needs commercial input). These may need escalation.\n\nLet me know if anything needs to be reprioritised.\n\nThanks\n\nUnresolved: DNS switch change window requirement; SLA credits for June outage (requires commercial input).\n\n## Decisions\n- Migration cutover moved to 28th, pending Fatima confirming with her infra team.\n\n## Actions\n| Action | Owner | Due |\n|--------|-------|-----|\n| Confirm migration cutover date of 28th with infra team | Fatima | Not set |\n| Chase network team for DR site firewall rules | Owner not assigned | Not set |\n| Follow up with procurement for the 4 licences PO | Rahul | Friday |\n| Send updated runbook | Ashish | Before cutover (28th) |\n\n## Follow-up email\n**Subject:** ADNOC Delivery Sync – Cutover Moved to 28th, Actions Needed\n\nHi Ashish, Priya, Rahul, Fatima,\n\nWe’ve moved the migration cutover to the 28th (Fatima to confirm with infra). Here are the actions from today:\n\n- Fatima: Confirm 28th cutover with your infra team.\n- Rahul: Follow up with procurement on the 4 licences PO by Friday. Budget is approved, but the PO hasn’t been received.\n- Ashish: Share the updated runbook before the cutover.\n- Firewall rules for the DR site: still missing, blocking the failover test. Someone needs to chase their network team—please assign or volunteer.\n\nTwo items are unresolved: whether the DNS switch requires a separate change window, and the SLA credits for the June outage (needs commercial input). These may need escalation.\n\nLet me know if anything needs to be reprioritised.\n\nThanks\n\nUnresolved: DNS switch change window requirement; SLA credits for June outage (requires commercial input).',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 07:57:49.502876','2026-08-20 07:58:56.405198',NULL,66902,'2026-08-20 07:57:49.171492');
